=== p2-windows · W7 · page:admin/BackupRestore (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:admin/BackupRestore   kind=page   web route=/backup
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/BackupRestorePage.tsx
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/BackupRestorePage/ (namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Admin)
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked. WinUI/maui-windows workload present.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection +
  parsers + registration, unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  AuditLogPage / GeofencesPage / ApiLogsPage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "BackupRestorePage.xaml + BackupRestorePageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these real
  conventions; the surface registers with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("BackupRestore", already in
  RouteTable.cs -> path "backup", RouteGroup.SettingsAccountIntegrations) via ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest record declares "no API data sources" (a gen-ui-prompts.ts miss — the web page
  in fact runs useQuery(['backup-configs']) -> GET /backup/configs and useQuery(['backup-runs']) -> GET /backup/runs
  plus seven mutations). To honour the parity covenant (no scope narrowing / no parity shortcuts) the native port
  implements the REAL data flow rather than the manifest's understated "local state" shape. The view-model reads both
  lists through an injected IBackupFeed; the default EmptyBackupFeed resolves the empty state (the sibling-page
  host-injection precedent), and the generated-client-backed BackupClientFeed (BackupRestorePage.Source.cs) binds to the
  generated OpenAPI contract operations get_api_v1_backup_configs (+create/{id} put/delete/{id}/trigger),
  get_api_v1_backup_runs, post_api_v1_backup_quick, post_api_v1_backup_runs_{id}_verify and
  get_api_v1_backup_runs_{id}_preview. All ten operations resolve against the generated endpoint table (asserted in
  BackupRestorePageTests.Every_bound_operation_resolves_against_the_generated_table). No HTTP touches the view; the list
  JSON round-trips through the tolerant BackupConfig.ParseList / BackupRun.ParseList parsers so the snake_case wire shape
  is preserved losslessly. Create/Update post the snake_case body (name/enabled/backup_type/frequency_days/
  max_retention/provider/provider_config/compress/encrypt) the Go handler reads.
- The four web data states render inside the PageContainer body as visible Fluent regions per ADR-006:
  loading -> stat + panel TsSkeleton shimmer (web `loading` skeleton row); error -> TsErrorDisplay + Retry
  (web `error={configsError}` PageContainer surface); empty -> per-panel TsEmptyState (web configs.length===0 /
  runs.length===0 with the "No backup configurations" + "New Config" CTA and "No backup runs yet"); success -> the
  populated configs/runs tables. The top-level BackupRestoreState (Loading/Empty/Error/Success) is the ledger/Narrator
  summary; per-panel visibility is still driven by the projected ShowConfigsEmpty/ShowRunsEmpty flags. Never a blank
  region.
- The two web GlassPanels (Backup Configurations, Backup History) are reproduced as TsGlassPanel/Mica regions, always
  visible. The four web MetricCards (Total Configs / Total Backups / Last Backup / Total Size) render as TsMetricCard
  tiles with the design-token accents (TsColorInfoBrush / TsColorSuccessBrush / TsChartPowerBrush / TsColorAccentBrush),
  no hardcoded colours. The configs + runs DataTables are composed from shared primitives (the web DataTable's rich
  cells — Badge, action buttons, schedule sub-rows — are not expressible by the text-only TsDataTable, so the row grid is
  built from TsBadge / TsButton / Caption exactly as the sibling AuditLogPage row composes its grid). Config row: name
  (+Disabled badge), type badge (Full/Incremental), provider chip (glyph+label), frequency (Daily / Every Nd), schedule
  (Last/Next), options (Compress/Encrypt badges) and the trigger/edit/delete actions. Run row: time, run-type badge,
  status (icon+badge, spinner on running), provider, file, size, records, duration and (for completed runs) the
  download/verify/preview actions. The recent-errors list (web failedRuns.slice(0,5)) renders the failed-run file/run
  label + error message in a danger-tinted card. The create/edit modal (TsModal) hosts the full form — name, enabled
  toggle, backup-type + frequency, max-retention + provider, the dynamic per-provider Provider Settings fields
  (local/s3/azure/gcs, web PROVIDER_FIELDS) and the compress/encrypt toggles. The delete confirm (TsConfirmDialog,
  destructive) and the restore-preview modal (TsModal: checksum badge + tables list, or the "No tables found" empty
  state) reproduce the remaining web surfaces. The Download action launches the absolute
  `${apiBase}/api/v1/backup/runs/{id}/download` URL via Windows.System.Launcher (web window.open parity); the
  BackupClientFeed resolves the base from ApiClientOptions.BaseAddress (null -> inert for the empty feed).
- SI units: backup file sizes are dimensionless bytes (no SI conversion) — formatted by the FormatBytes port that
  matches the web formatBytes (B/KB/MB/GB/TB, 1 decimal <10, rounded >=10, invariant culture). Counts format through
  FormatInt (web fmtInt / Intl.NumberFormat), relative times through FormatRelative (web formatRelative tiers:
  "just now"/"Nm ago"/"Nh ago"/"Nd ago"/absolute), durations through FormatDurationMsCompact (web
  formatDurationMsCompact: ms/s/m). `now` is injected so relative output is deterministic in tests.
- All 81 i18n keys resolve through the ILocalizer facade with the verbatim web key names, in one BackupRestoreText.Resolve
  bundle the projection touches on every projection regardless of data state (asserted by
  Projection_resolves_every_required_string_key + _even_in_the_loading_state). The translation.backup.* / common.* /
  error.loadFailed keys already exist in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw (added by an earlier W-step), so no catalog
  edit was required. The WinUI TextBox.PlaceholderText property (2 sites) and the web i18n key name
  backup.configNamePlaceholder (1 site) carry inline `// parity:allow` markers (WinUI API / web key name, not stub
  placeholders).
- W1 materialization: the generated C# client (apps/windows/Generated) was absent from the worktree, so the whole
  solution failed to build at baseline (CS0234: TeslaSync.Windows.* missing). Regenerated it via
  `pwsh apps/tools/codegen/gen-clients.ps1` (wrote Generated/Api/*.cs) and scaffolded the Generated/Generated.csproj
  (modelled on apps/tools/codegen/verify/csharp/Verify.csproj: net10.0, Nullable, in-box System.Text.Json, compiles
  Api/*.cs) that TeslaSync.App.Core references. Both are build artifacts, NOT committed by this task. Baseline then went
  green (0 errors). The BackupRestorePage Model/Source/ViewModel are linked into TeslaSync.App.Tests via <Compile
  Include> (the WinExe cannot be project-referenced), exactly as the sibling page test fixtures are.

